# ==============================================================================
# EduSmart-AI Backend CVE Exceptions
# Verified non-exploitable / unreachable in CampusCore architecture
# Full justification documented in docs/security/CI_SECURITY_GATES.md Section 5
# ==============================================================================

# Vulnerability ID: CVE-2026-47884
# Package: org.springframework:spring-webmvc
# Scope: backend (Spring MVC transitive dependency via spring-boot-starter-web)
# Owner: Sathu (Lead Security Engineer)
# Review Date: 2026-11-20
# Next Review Date: 2027-02-20
# Justification: Remote Code Execution via XsltView path traversal in Spring Web.
# Reachability Analysis: UNREACHABLE. CampusCore is architected strictly as a headless JSON REST API (@RestController).
# No XsltView, XsltViewResolver, or XSLT stylesheet templates exist in the codebase.
# Remediation Conditions: Upgrade to Spring Framework 7.x or backported 6.2.x patch release when officially published.
CVE-2026-47884

# Vulnerability ID: CVE-2026-47890
# Package: org.springframework:spring-webmvc
# Scope: backend (Spring MVC transitive dependency via spring-boot-starter-web)
# Owner: Sathu (Lead Security Engineer)
# Review Date: 2026-11-20
# Next Review Date: 2027-02-20
# Justification: Stream corruption in Server-Sent Events (SSE) combined with view-rendering contexts.
# Reachability Analysis: UNREACHABLE. CampusCore does not implement Server-Sent Events (SseEmitter) with view templates.
# Remediation Conditions: Upgrade to Spring Framework 7.x or backported 6.2.x patch release when officially published.
CVE-2026-47890
